    title: "TEENAGE ENTREPRENEURS",
    text: "The emergence of young entrepreneurs as significant economic actors has attracted considerable media attention and investment interest in recent years. Digital technology has dramatically lowered the barriers to starting a business, enabling young people with ideas, energy, and technical skills to reach global markets from their bedrooms. Critics caution against romanticising teenage entrepreneurship, noting that success stories represent a tiny fraction of attempts and that young founders face unique challenges related to inexperience, limited networks, and the demands of balancing business with education. Nevertheless, the entrepreneurial instinct is widely recognised as a valuable capacity worth nurturing at any age.",
